From 19215d640389f23eb545510a59793bc53f4a8096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:21:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Invite player: a quiet button by the join requests, off
 the table column

The Invite a Player Back slip lay under Pass notes in the Lightkeeper's
table column on every view, though it is wanted once in a blue moon. It
is now a small moonlit text button, "Invite player", where people come
into the campaign: under the join requests, centred as they are, or once
the circle is finalized under the sealed slip, where the requests were.
Pressed, it lays the same username form under itself on a small slip,
with a line saying the player rejoins with a new investigator without
waiting for approval; Escape puts it away. The field is 16px and the
button and Send invite 44px on a touch screen, and a second Send waits
for the first. The table column (dice, log, pass notes) no longer holds
it on any size.

Checked in Chromium on a campaign with a request waiting and on a
finalized one, at 1440x900, 1366x768 and 1920x1080 and on a phone
(390x844) and a tablet (820x1180) with touch: the button lies under the
requests or the sealed slip and never in the dice column, opens the form
with the field focused, an unknown name shows the server's reason, a real
one says "Invite sent to" the name, Escape closes it and focuses the
button, and no page scrolls sideways. DESIGN.md says where it lies.

